// scrypt, RFC 7914:
// https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc7914
//
// A password stretched into a key that costs memory as well as time, which is
// what makes a guess at a password expensive for whoever is guessing. The
// sequential pass over a large buffer is the part that resists a machine built
// out of cheap parallel cores.
//
// Salsa20/8 and the PBKDF2 wrapper are here rather than taken from a library:
// the first is a step of this construction and not a cipher anything should
// reach for, and the second is only ever called with one round, where its role
// is to spread the password across the initial buffer.
//
// Not here: the higher-level formats that wrap scrypt with their own salt and
// parameters. This is the function of RFC 7914 §5, nothing on top.
import {
  "moonbitstack/mooncrypt/hash/sha2",
  "moonbitstack/mooncrypt/kdf/pbkdf2",
  "moonbitstack/mooncrypt/spec",
}

import {
  "moonbitlang/core/encoding/hex",
  "moonbitlang/core/encoding/utf8",
} for "test"
